<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The mech resurrector's idle crackle: the red sparks of Biotech's ApocrionAttached (sic,
    Biotech Defs/Effects/Effecter_Misc.xml), the apocriton's always-on CompEffecter, without
    its second child, the Mote_ApocritonPulse psychic wave, which is the apocriton's hatred
    aura and no part of a mech resurrector. Played on the armor's wearer by
    OverlordWarcasket.CompResurrectorSparks (Source/1.6/Comps/), which gates it on the resurrector
    holding a charge and the wearer being able to cast; its header has the conditions and the tick
    path.

    The spark child is the apocriton's with three fields changed. Biotech draws the apocriton
    at drawSize 2 and a humanlike body at 1.5, so the spark scale 1.0~1.2 becomes 0.8~1.0.
    positionRadius stays the apocriton's 0.7, which suits the art rather than the mesh:
    SubEffecter_Sprayer places each spark uniformly in an annulus between positionRadiusMin and
    positionRadius around the wearer (Rand.InsideAnnulusVector3, 1.7.4990 decompile), and the
    Overlord's shell fills nearly its whole 1.5-cell canvas, about 0.68 cells from the centre to
    its sides and 0.83 to the shoulder pads' tips. 0.7 lets the sparks reach the shell's sides,
    where they read against the ground, while most still land on the plating and none stray far
    past the shoulder pads. positionRadiusMin 0.1, which the apocriton leaves at 0, keeps them
    off the wearer's exact centre. chancePerTick 0.01 at a burst of 1~2 is a burst every 100
    ticks on average at random gaps, two thirds of the apocriton's 0.015: a pilot's readied
    resurrector crackles less than a mech built around one. The spark frequency mod setting
    overrides chancePerTick, shown as a percent of the apocriton's (this default, 67%).
  -->
  <EffecterDef>
    <defName>OLWC_ResurrectorSparks</defName>
    <children>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerChance</subEffecterClass>
        <moteDef>Mote_MechSparkSimple</moteDef>
        <burstCount>1~2</burstCount>
        <chancePerTick>0.01</chancePerTick>
        <rotation>-150~-150</rotation>
        <spawnLocType>OnTarget</spawnLocType>
        <scale>0.8~1.0</scale>
        <positionRadiusMin>0.1</positionRadiusMin>
        <positionRadius>0.7</positionRadius>
        <attachToSpawnThing>true</attachToSpawnThing>
        <rotateTowardsTargetCenter>true</rotateTowardsTargetCenter>
      </li>
    </children>
  </EffecterDef>
</Defs>
